+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What county is Pawleys Island in?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Georgetown County, both the island and the mainland that shares its name. Its property taxes and its public schools are Georgetown County's."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Pawleys Island part of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The island is its own town, and the mainland around it is run by Georgetown County. Broadway at the Beach, in Myrtle Beach, is about 26 miles north by road."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the ZIP code for Pawleys Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"29585. It covers the island and most of the mainland around it, from the beach to well west of US 17."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many people live on Pawleys Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Census counted 130 people living in the town in 2020. Most island houses are second homes or rentals, so far more people stay in the summer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Pawleys Island expensive?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the island, yes: over three years a house sold for about $2.45 million at the middle. On the mainland, a house sold for about $580,000 to $675,000 at the middle in the past year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you drive a golf cart on Pawleys Island?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, on island roads. The cart needs a state registration and a town sticker, and the address on its registration must be within 2 miles of the town limits. The driver must be 16 or older with a license. No driving at night or in the rain."}}]}</script>
