-</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Pawleys Island is a barrier island, less than 4 miles long and mostly one house wide. Two short causeways, the North Causeway and the South Causeway, cross the salt marsh to the mainland.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Town of Pawleys Island is the island itself. The mainland around it shares its name and ZIP code and is run by Georgetown County.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 1603" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-map-t"><title id="c3-pi-map-t">Aerial map of Pawleys Island, South Carolina, and the mainland around it. The island is a thin strip along the ocean with salt marsh behind it; the town limits are shaded and outlined. Two causeways cross the marsh to the mainland. US 17 runs inland, parallel to the coast. Litchfield is north of the island on the ocean side of US 17; the mainland behind the island lies between US 17 and the marsh; about 4,800 houses are west of US 17.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-area-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="1603" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M538.3 1492.4L538.9 1482.1L547 1462.9L552.4 1452.1L566.8 1435.5L573.2 1421.9L578.8 1407.4L589 1386.4L596.2 1366.7L605.3 1345.7L613.3 1329.7L617.2 1319.8L619.2 1312.3L621.9 1298.1L623.1 1285.7L622 1275.4L618.3 1261.3L605.2 1246.5L603.6 1243.3L602.4 1240.2L601.8 1235.1L603.5 1229.8L607.7 1224.3L612.1 1220L624.4 1211.1L636.7 1205.3L681.6 1188L687.8 1183.5L691.2 1178.4L692.8 1173L693.3 1165.7L691.2 1158.6L688.9 1156L687 1151.8L686.5 1146.6L684.4 1140.2L684.8 1134.5L684.1 1131.8L686.5 1129.3L689.5 1128.8L692.8 1130.7L694.9 1130.4L699 1128.2L703.3 1123.6L705.3 1120L705.8 1116.5L705.7 1107L702.5 1098.9L698.4 1095.8L683.7 1096.5L680.6 1094.8L679.2 1092.3L678.1 1086.7L674.4 1083.4L675.5