 houses between the ocean and the creek. About 220 houses face the beach. Across the island, only about 1 in 5 houses is its owner's main home.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Pawleys Island, labelled: the North Causeway crossing the salt marsh from the mainland to the island, a narrow strip of houses, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Pawleys Island at the North Causeway from above: the salt marsh, the causeway, and the rows of houses between the marsh and the beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Beach parking is free, the speed limit is 25 mph, and the town still calls itself "arrogantly shabby".</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="1600" alt="A wooden walkway with a small roofed platform over a tidal creek and marsh grass on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A walkway and a covered platform over the creek on the marsh side of Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Over three years an island house sold for about $2.45 million at the middle, more on the ocean and less on the creek side. At our last count, only 2 were for sale, each asking about $3 million or more.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Send me the Pawleys Island houses for sale now<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="litchfield" class="c3-pi-place">Litchfield<span>The beach north of the island, and more houses for sale</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North of the island, Litchfield runs along the beach on the ocean side of the highway. It has about 1,200 houses, and about 4 in 10 are their owner's main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More houses sell here: 50 in the past year, at about $1.25 million at the middle. Its oceanfront houses sold for about $3.6 million at the middle over three years. Almost all of its ocean side is in a high-risk flood zone too.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Farther north are Huntington Beach State Park, with Atalaya, the old winter home of Archer and Anna Hyatt Huntington, and their Brookgreen Gardens. Together they are a National Historic Landmark.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Litchfield">Get the homes for sale in Litchfield<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="behind-the-island" class="c3-pi-place">The mainland behind the island<span>Shops, groceries and golf near the causeways</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Between the highway and the marsh, south of Litchfield, are about 1,200 houses, and most are their owner's main home. The Hammock Shops, two grocery stores and Pawleys Plantation's golf course are here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here sold for about $675,000 at the middle in the past year, and about a third are in a high-risk flood zone. A house with a homeowners association comes with its rules on rentals and changes, and we read its papers for you.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale behind Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-of-17" class="c3-pi-place">West of US 17<span>Most of the homes, most of the golf, the lowest prices</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of US 17 are most of the homes with a Pawleys Island address: about 4,800 houses, most of them their owner's main home. We count nine golf courses here, among them Caledonia, True Blue, Heritage and Litchfield Country Club.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here sold for about $580,000 at the middle in the past year, and a condo for about $320,000, the lowest prices of the four parts. Only about 1 in 20 houses is in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale west of US 17 in Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything from the island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car, without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 adds time.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From Town Hall to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The nearest grocery store, on US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Under 5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Hammock Shops, on US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Huntington Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Brookgreen Gardens</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Downtown Georgetown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">40 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach, Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">40 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Downtown Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1 hr 45 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="how-often"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How often one sells">How often does a house on Pawleys Island come up for sale?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rarely. In the past five years at least 44 of the island's houses were bought at a market price, about 1 in 11. In Litchfield and west of the highway, houses were bought about twice as often.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses bought at a market price in the past five years"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses bought at a market price in the past five years</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.368" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 11</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.74" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.784" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>At least: the county keeps only the last deed on each house, so a house sold and later deeded to a trust counts as not sold. That is true in every part. Georgetown County records; a market sale is a deed of $10,000 or more.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Island houses tend to stay in families. On most, the last recorded transfer was not a sale but a deed under $1,000, the kind used to pass a house to heirs or a trust.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses whose last recorded transfer was not a sale"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses whose last recorded transfer was not a sale</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.615" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 6 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.405" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.329" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 3</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The last deed on the house shows under $1,000. Georgetown County records.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town says many houses in its historic district belong to the third, fourth or fifth generation of one family. About 1 in 10 has not changed hands since before 2000, and only about a dozen new buildings went up in seven years. The house you want can come up once in years.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="taxes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly costs">What does a Pawleys Island house cost to own each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The biggest yearly costs are property tax and flood insurance. Both depend most on whether the house is your main home.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Property tax</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">As a second home or rental, a house pays about 3 times the property tax it pays as your main home. South Carolina taxes a main home on 4 percent of its value and any other house on 6 percent, at about twice the rate.</p><div class="c3-pi-tax"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Price</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Main home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Second home</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$580,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,740</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$8,350</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$900,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,150</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$12,850</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,450,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$11,220</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$34,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The first price is the middle sale west of the highway, and the last is the island's. The town levies no property tax of its own.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood insurance</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take an island house that is not its owner's main home. Its federal flood policy cost more than 4 times one on a mainland house in the same ZIP code. As a main home, the gap is much smaller. The prices include the town's 25 percent discount.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">House</span><span role="columnheader">A year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, not the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,770</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.353" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,680</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mainland house, same ZIP code</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.22" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,050</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>FEMA's flood insurance policies on single-family houses that began in the 12 months to May 2026, ZIP 29585. Island: the Town of Pawleys Island's policies. Mainland: the Georgetown County policies in the same ZIP code. The cost includes FEMA's fees.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most island policies cover the building for $250,000, the most the federal program pays on a home, so a house worth more needs private flood coverage too. We get wind and homeowners quotes before you offer, and our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> explains them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: the island's middle house as a second home</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">As a second home or rental, the island's middle house costs about $39,700 a year before the mortgage and before wind and homeowners insurance.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax as a second home, with the $44 in fees</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$34,900</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A federal flood policy, the middle for an island house that is not a main home</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,770</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Together</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$39,700</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the yearly cost of the Pawleys house you like</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its tax as a main home and a second home, and get its insurance quotes before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out a house's yearly cost</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you rent out a house on Pawleys Island, and what do rentals take in?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Short-term rentals are allowed on Pawleys Island. Guests pay about 11 percent in lodging taxes on stays under 90 days.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden walkway over green dunes leading to the ocean on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A wooden walkway over the dunes to the beach on Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's lodging tax receipts show what island rentals take in. In 2024, guests paid about $27 million to stay on the island. Spread across the roughly 380 island houses that are not an owner's main home, that is about $70,000 a house for the year, before fees and other costs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That is an average: some houses are never rented, and some rent is paid on condos and other rooms. More than half of the lodging tax dollars came in from July to September, and little from January to March.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rules town by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>. To weigh rent against price, see <a href="/invest/rental-returns/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what return a rental should make</a>, or our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">long-term rental guide</a> for a yearly tenant.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding and storms">Does Pawleys Island flood, and how often do hurricanes come?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every island house but one is in one of FEMA's high-risk flood zones, so a lender will require flood insurance. The houses are split about evenly between two zones:</p><ul class="c3-pi-rules"><li><strong>About half: the VE zone</strong>Rising water and storm waves are both expected.</li><li><strong>The other half: the AE zone</strong>Water rises in a big flood, but big waves are not expected.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The south end is the most exposed. South of the South Causeway, nearly every house is in the VE zone. North of the North Causeway, few are.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-north-end-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-north-end-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-north-end-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wide beach at low tide with a row of raised houses along the dunes and an inlet beyond" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>The north end of Pawleys Island at low tide: houses along the dune line, and the inlet at right.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA's flood height for island houses is 12 to 16 feet above a fixed survey level, not the depth of water at a house. A new house's floor must sit 3 feet above it. Day to day, king tides put water on the island's roads.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Hurricanes</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past 75 years, 44 storms have passed within 50 miles of the middle of the island, and 7 were hurricanes at their closest point. Ian passed about 5 miles away, and Matthew and Charley came closer still.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-pi-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Storms that passed within 50 miles of the island, by decade</span><svg class="c3-pi-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 240" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of storms whose center passed within 50 miles of Pawleys Island, by decade: 1950s 5 storms, 2 hurricanes; 1960s 5 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1970s 2 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1980s 4 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1990s 4 storms, 0 hurricanes; 2000s 8 storms, 1 hurricanes; 2010s 8 storms, 2 hurricanes; 2020s 8 storms, 2 hurricanes."><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="196" y2="196" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="28" y="202" text-anchor="end">0</text><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="111" y2="111" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="28" y="117" text-anchor="end">5</text><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="26" y2="26" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="28" y="32" text-anchor="end">10</text><rect x="39.6" y="111" width="28.6" height="85" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="39.6" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="53.9" y="105" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text x="53.9" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’50</text><rect x="79.3" y="111" width="28.6" height="85" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="93.6" y="105" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text x="93.6" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’60</text><rect x="119.1" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="133.4" y="156" text-anchor="middle">2</text><text x="133.4" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’70</text><rect x="158.8" y="128" width="28.6" height="68" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="173.1" y="122" text-anchor="middle">4</text><text x="173.1" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’80</text><rect x="198.6" y="128" width="28.6" height="68" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="212.9" y="122" text-anchor="middle">4</text><text x="212.9" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’90</text><rect x="238.3" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="238.3" y="179" width="28.6" height="17" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="252.6" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="252.6" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’00</text><rect x="278.1" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="278.1" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="292.4" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="292.4" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’10</text><rect x="317.8" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="317.8" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="332.1" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="332.1" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’20</text></svg><ul class="c3-pi-names" aria-label="The seven hurricanes"><li>Hazel, 1954</li><li>Helene, 1958</li><li>Charley, 2004</li><li>Matthew, 2016</li><li>Dorian, 2019</li><li>Isaias, 2020</li><li>Ian, 2022</li></ul><figcaption>Each column is a decade, from the 1950s (’50) to the 2020s (’20). Darker: storms that were hurricanes at their closest point. NOAA National Hurricane Center storm tracks (HURDAT2), 1950 to 2025, measured from the middle of the island.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hurricane Hazel, in 1954, washed away most of the houses built on the south end after World War II. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">hurricane guide</a> covers the rest of the coast.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the flood zone and floor height of one Pawleys house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We look up its flood zone, VE or AE, and how high its floor is above the flood height on FEMA's map.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a house's flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="rebuild"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rebuilding and old houses">Can you rebuild or change a house on Pawleys Island?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, within limits that matter most at the south end. The state's baseline follows the top of the front dune, and its setback line runs 20 feet behind it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On about 100 of the island's oceanfront houses, nearly half, part of the house stands past the setback line, most of them at the south end. On Litchfield's oceanfront it is more than half.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig narrow"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-inset" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="650 250 850 900" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-inset-t"><title id="c3-pi-inset-t">Aerial map of the south end of Pawleys Island: one row of oceanfront houses between the creek and the beach. The state's baseline along the top of the front dune and its setback line 20 feet behind it run through the row of houses. A shaded house has part of it on the ocean side of the setback line.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-south-end-aerial-1000.webp" x="650" y="250" width="850" height="900" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1383.2 -50.9L1376.4 -38.1L1377 -37.7L1368.8 -22.6L1370 -22.2L1366.9 -16.5L1379 -9.8L1381.5 -15.2L1406.5 -1.7L1412.4 -13.1L1416.9 -10.8L1414.1 -5.4L1416.9 -4L1418.3 -6.4L1430.2 0L1433 -5.1L1413.8 -15.2L1415.3 -17.9L1409.3 -20.9L1409.9 -21.9L1408.5 -22.6L1414.7 -34.4L1383.2 -50.9Z" fill="rgba(196,120,58,.5)" stroke="#ffb35c" stroke-width="4"/><path 