e="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="9"/><path d="M1467.6 -168.4L1445.3 -113.9L1427.6 -63.3L1390.8 17.5L1390.5 17.9M1390.5 17.9L1372.2 60.3L1335.7 145.5L1316 186.3M1316 186.3L1286.2 248.9L1285.9 249.6L1246.8 333.1L1207.7 417.3L1175.3 498.2L1158.2 540.6L1117.7 637.3L1092.4 683.5L1065.4 729.3L1064.2 731.3L1045.7 773.4L1008 855.6L969.2 939.4L930.4 1023.7L891.8 1107.5L871.6 1150.3L831.7 1233.8L791.7 1317.4L751.8 1400.9L712.1 1484.1L672.2 1567.6L632 1651.2L592.3 1734.7L568.7 1760.6L554.1 1771.8L538.9 1766.7L509.6 1752.2L475.6 1727L471.9 1724.9" fill="none" stroke="#ffd27a" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="16 10"/><path d="M464.6 1741.8L500.3 1768L531.8 1783.9L557.7 1792.6L581.3 1774.4L607.8 1745.1M607.8 1745.1L647.4 1661.6L687.7 1578.1L727.3 1494.5L767.2 1411.3L806.9 1327.8L847.1 1244.3L887.1 1160.7L908.4 1115.6L947.2 1031.4L986.1 947.5L1024.6 863.3L1062.8 781.1L1081.1 738.7L1108.4 692.5L1134.3 645.4L1175.3 547.7L1192.5 505.3L1224.8 424.1L1263.9 340.2L1302.7 256.7L1352.5 153.3L1389.1 68L1407.7 24.6L1444.5 -56.6L1462.8 -107.8L1487.5 -168.4" fill="none" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="9"/><path d="M464.6 1741.8L500.3 1768L531.8 1783.9L557.7 1792.6L581.3 1774.4L607.8 1745.1M607.8 1745.1L647.4 1661.6L687.7 1578.1L727.3 1494.5L767.2 1411.3L806.9 1327.8L847.1 1244.3L887.1 1160.7L908.4 1115.6L947.2 1031.4L986.1 947.5L1024.6 863.3L1062.8 781.1L1081.1 738.7L1108.4 692.5L1134.3 645.4L1175.3 547.7L1192.5 505.3L1224.8 424.1L1263.9 340.2L1302.7 256.7L1352.5 153.3L1389.1 68L1407.7 24.6L1444.5 -56.6L1462.8 -107.8L1487.5 -168.4" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="5"/><path d="M1045.7 773.4L1125.7 718.4" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="1045.7" cy="773.4" r="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="4"/><text class="lb sb" x="1133.7" y="663.4">Setback</text><text class="lb sb" x="1133.7" y="721.4">line</text><path d="M986.1 947.5L1076.1 967.5" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="986.1" cy="947.5" r="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="4"/><text class="lb" x="1084.1" y="987.5">Top of</text><text class="lb" x="1084.1" y="1043.5">the dune</text><text class="lb" x="1084.1" y="1099.5">(baseline)</text></svg></div><ul class="c3-pi-legend"><li><i style="background:rgba(196,120,58,.75);border:2px solid #ffb35c"></i>Part of the house, about 200 square feet or more, is past the setback line</li><li><i style="background:rgba(255,255,255,.6);border:2px solid #8a96a3"></i>The house is behind it</li></ul><figcaption>A stretch of the south end of the island, north of the south-end parking lot. Lines: the state's current baseline and setback line. Outlines: Georgetown County's 2024 building footprints. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a house past the setback line, state law allows:</p><ul class="c3-pi-rules"><li><strong>Repair</strong>A house a storm damages but does not destroy can be repaired.</li><li><strong>Rebuild</strong>A house a storm destroys can be rebuilt, never past the baseline. Past the setback line it can be no larger, no wider along the beach and no farther toward the ocean than before.</li><li><strong>New house</strong>Built partly past the setback line, it can have at most 5,000 square feet of heated space.</li><li><strong>The town's own line</strong>The town's Shore Protection Line is usually stricter than the state's.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer on an oceanfront house, we read its survey to see where all three lines fall on the lot.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The old houses and the town's historic list</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The whole island is now a local historic district. A house built in 1954 or earlier can be nominated for the town's list of historic houses, even without its owner asking. A listed house needs the board's approval to change its outside or be torn down, and the listing stays with it. We check whether a house you like is listed.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pawleys-island-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Pawleys Island FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What county is Pawleys Island in?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Georgetown County, both the island and the mainland that shares its name. Schools are assigned by address in the Georgetown County School District.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Pawleys Island part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The island is its own town, with its own police department. Broadway at the Beach, in Myrtle Beach, is about 26 miles north by road.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the ZIP code for Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">29585, for the island and most of the mainland around it, to well west of the highway.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live on Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Census counted 130 people living in the town in 2020. Far more people stay in the summer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart on Pawleys Island?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on island roads, with a state registration and a town sticker. The driver must be 16 or older with a license, and carts may not be driven at night or in the rain.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://gis1.georgetowncountysc.org/portal/rest/services" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/385/Property-Tax-Calculator" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax calculator</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/profile/Pawleys_Island_town,_South_Carolina?g=160XX00US4555015" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/api/open/v3/NfipPolicies" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/#hurdat" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">storm tracks</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t48c039.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">beachfront law</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax law</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c036.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lodging tax law</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax rates</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/72001211" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Register</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/about-pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/2026-Annual-Budget-FINAL.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town budget</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Pawleys-Island-Atax-Agenda_Packet-Nov-2025-1.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lodging tax</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/passed-ordinances/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ordinances</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/2025-legal-settlement-faqs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">inlet settlement</a>, <a href="https://southcarolinaparks.com/huntington-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">state park</a>, <a href="https://hammockshops.com/pages/history" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hammock Shops</a>, <a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/land-based-station/us-climate-normals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA normals</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/climo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NHC</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/dogs-on-the-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dog rules</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/84002045" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brookgreen</a>, <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap</a>. Our counts: county parcels, footprints, flood zones, deeds; CCMLS listings in aggregate; OpenStreetMap places; drives without traffic. Tax: county estimate with fees ($44 island, $96 west of US 17).</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Pawleys Island at the North Causeway from above: the salt marsh, the causeway, and the rows of houses between the marsh and the beach. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">A walkway over the dunes on Pawleys Island. Photo: Phoebe, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, 