-walkway-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":1600,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"A walkway and a covered platform over the creek on the marsh side of Pawleys Island","caption":"A walkway and a covered platform over the creek on the marsh side of Pawleys Island.","description":"A wooden walkway with a small roofed platform over a tidal creek and marsh grass on Pawleys Island","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Phoebe"},"creditText":"Phoebe, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Phoebe, CC BY-SA 4.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marsh_walkway_Pawleys.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marsh_walkway_Pawleys.jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Pawleys Island, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true},{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-north-end-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-north-end-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The north end of Pawleys Island at low tide: houses along the dune line, and the inlet at right","caption":"The north end of Pawleys Island at low tide: houses along the dune line, and the inlet at right.","description":"A wide beach at low tide with a row of raised houses along the dunes and an inlet beyond","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Phoebe"},"creditText":"Phoebe, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Phoebe, CC BY-SA 4.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pawleys_Island_North_End.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pawleys_Island_North_End.jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Pawleys Island, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Island or mainland, we check four things before you offer.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">The flood zone and how high the floor sits. Where the setback line falls on an oceanfront lot. Whether the town lists the house as historic. The tax bill as your main home or a second home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Talk to a Pawleys Island agent</a></div></section></main>
+</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Pawleys Island is a barrier island, less than 4 miles long and mostly one house wide, with salt marsh between it and the mainland. Two short causeways, the North Causeway and the South Causeway, cross the marsh.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Town of Pawleys Island is the island itself. The mainland around it has no town government; it is run by Georgetown County. Much of it shares the island's name and its ZIP code, 29585, so a Pawleys Island address can be a house on the mainland. This page covers four parts, from the beach inland.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 1603" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-map-t"><title id="c3-pi-map-t">Aerial map of Pawleys Island, South Carolina, and the mainland around it. The island is a thin strip along the ocean with salt marsh behind it; the town limits are shaded and outlined. Two causeways cross the marsh to the mainland. US 17 runs inland, parallel to the coast. Litchfield is north of the island on the ocean side of US 17; the mainland behind the island lies between US 17 and the marsh; about 4,800 houses are west of US 17.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-area-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="1603" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M538.3 1492.4L538.9 1482.1L547 1462.9L552.4 1452.1L566.8 1435.5L573.2 1421.9L578.8 1407.4L589 1386.4L596.2 1366.7L605.3 1345.7L613.3 1329.7L617.2 1319.8L619.2 1312.3L621.9 1298.1L623.1 1285.7L622 1275.4L618.3 1261.3L605.2 1246.5L603.6 1243.3L602.4 1240.2L601.8 1235.1L603.5 1229.8L607.7 1224.3L612.1 1220L624.4 1211.1L636.7 1205.3L681.6 1188L687.8 1183.5L691.2 1178.4L692.8 1173L693.3 1165.7L691.2 1158.6L688.9 1156L687 1151.8L686.5 1146.6L684.4 1140.2L684.8 1134.5L684.1 1131.8L686.5 1129.3L689