64.3 701.8L775.5 682.2M740.2 732.3L757.2 712.6M838.4 572L847.5 556M847.5 556L851.7 548.8M353.7 944.5L363.8 940.5M587.6 822.1L597.8 816.7M584.5 823.8L587.6 822.1M509 864.4L532.8 851.5M914.4 438.6L916.4 435.1M994.5 295.8L999.4 286.6M990.7 302.9L994.5 295.8M1036 217.9L1044.6 202.1M1044.6 202.1L1047.5 196.6M444.8 899L452.5 894.9M786.2 663.7L790.6 656.1M1004.7 276.6L1005.6 274.9M775.5 682.2L776.4 680.8M-202.3 1217.3L-88.4 1116.2M-88.4 1116.2L-76.8 1106.6L-64.9 1098.4L-50 1090.3L-41 1086.6" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".95" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M788.8 776.4L817.5 818.1M817.5 818.1L835.5 833.8M770 758.7L781.3 769M781.3 769L788.8 776.4M761 750.4L770 758.7M740.3 732.4L761 750.4M665 971L760.9 1009.2M662 969.4L665 971M643.1 959.6L662 969.4M632.3 953.9L643.1 959.6M625.2 950.1L632.3 953.9M622.1 948.5L625.2 950.1M554.3 912.9L622.1 948.5M543.7 908.4L554.3 912.9M509.8 903L530 904.8L543.7 908.4M508.2 902.9L509.8 903M444.8 899L463.5 899.4L508.2 902.9" fill="none" stroke="#f2b25c" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><text class="lb it sm" x="1166.7" y="1454" text-anchor="middle">Atlantic Ocean</text><text class="lb sm" x="846.7" y="466.2" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-57 846.7 466.2)">US 17</text><text class="lb hl" x="917.8" y="1081.3" text-anchor="start" transform="rotate(-52 917.8 1081.3)">Pawleys Island</text><text class="lb" x="1275.6" y="149.2" text-anchor="end">Litchfield</text><text class="lb" x="77.8" y="1230.4" text-anchor="start">Behind the island</text><text class="lb" x="77.8" y="410.2" text-anchor="start">West of US 17</text></svg></div><figcaption>The shaded strip inside the dashed line is the Town of Pawleys Island: the island and the marsh behind it. The orange lines are the two causeways. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Lines: Georgetown County GIS. Labels: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><h3 id="the-island" class="c3-pi-place">Pawleys Island, the town<span>The beach in front, the creek behind</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The island is one long strip of houses between the ocean and the creek. About 220 houses face the beach. The rest look onto the marsh and the creek, or stand on the streets between. In the middle of the island are the old wooden summer houses of the historic district.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-at-the-north-causeway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Pawleys Island, labelled: the North Causeway crossing the salt marsh from the mainland to the island, a narrow strip of houses, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Pawleys Island at the North Causeway from above: the salt marsh, the causeway, and the rows of houses between the marsh and the beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The water is close on both sides. People fish in the surf and crab from the two marsh bridges, and the island has three boat ramps. Beach parking is free: the south-end lot is the largest free beach lot in Georgetown County, and 8 other public accesses add about 141 spaces. Dogs are allowed on the beach all year, on a leash on summer days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pace is slow. The speed limit is 25 mph, and golf carts are allowed on island roads. There are no lifeguards and no fireworks. The town still calls itself by its old nickname, "arrogantly shabby".</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="1600" alt="A wooden walkway with a small roofed platform over a tidal creek and marsh grass on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A walkway and a covered platform over the creek on the marsh side of Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Over three years an island house sold for about $2.45 million at the middle, more on the ocean and less on the creek side. At our last count, only 2 island houses were for sale, each asking about $3 million or more.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Send me the Pawleys Island houses for sale now<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="litchfield" class="c3-pi-place">Litchfield<span>The beach north of the island, and more houses for sale</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North of the island, Litchfield runs along the beach on the ocean side of the highway. It has about 1,200 houses, and more of them are lived in all year: about 4 in 10 are their owner's main home, twice the island's share.</p><ul class="c3-pi-rules" aria-label="Near Litchfield"><li><strong>A bike path</strong>The Waccamaw Neck Bikeway runs along US 17 through Litchfield and north to Murrells Inlet.</li><li><strong>Huntington Beach State Park</strong>Farther north: 3 miles of beach, and Atalaya, the old winter home of Archer and Anna Hyatt Huntington.</li><li><strong>Brookgreen Gardens</strong>Opposite the park. The Huntingtons set it up as a nature preserve to show her sculpture and the work of other sculptors.</li><li><strong>A landmark</strong>Atalaya and Brookgreen Gardens together are a National Historic Landmark.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More houses sell here: 50 in the past year, at about $1.25 million at the middle. Its oceanfront houses sell for more than the island's: about $3.6 million at the middle over three years. Almost all of Litchfield's ocean side is in a high-risk flood zone too.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Litchfield">Get the homes for sale in Litchfield<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="behind-the-island" class="c3-pi-place">The mainland behind the island<span>Shops, groceries and golf near the causeways</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Between US 17 and the marsh, south of Litchfield, are about 1,200 houses, and most are their owner's main home. This is where the island shops, a few minutes by car from Town Hall.</p><ul class="c3-pi-rules" aria-label="Behind the island"><li><strong>The Hammock Shops</strong>On the highway near the North Causeway: more than 20 shops and two restaurants, Local and BisQit.</li><li><strong>Groceries</strong>Two grocery stores on the highway.</li><li><strong>Golf</strong>Pawleys Plantation has its own course.</li><li><strong>A bike path</strong>The Waccamaw Neck Bikeway runs north from here.</li></ul><aside class="c3-pi-note"><strong>The Pawleys Island hammock</strong>The Hammock Shops take their name from the Original Hammock Shop, which has made them since 1938. They say a riverboat captain who carried rice between Georgetown and Waverly Mills made the first one in 1889, to sleep cooler on summer nights. It was woven of cotton rope, with no thick knots where he lay. The shops still sell handmade hammocks.</aside><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house in a community with a homeowners association comes with the association's rules on rentals and changes, and we read its papers for you.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here sold for about $675,000 at the middle in the past year. About a third of the houses are in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale behind Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-of-17" class="c3-pi-place">West of US 17<span>Most of the homes, most of the golf, the lowest prices</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of US 17 are most of the homes with a Pawleys Island address: about 4,800 houses, and most are their owner's main home. Most of the area's golf courses are here. We count nine on the map, among them Caledonia, True Blue, Heritage and Litchfield Country Club.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The grocery store nearest the island is on this side of the highway, less than 5 minutes by car from Town Hall. Only about 1 in 20 houses here is in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house here sold for about $580,000 at the middle in the past year, and a condo for about $320,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Get the homes for sale west of US 17 in Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="living"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Living there all year">What is it like to live on Pawleys Island all year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Winter on the island is quiet. On Census Day, in April, most of the island's homes were seasonal or vacation homes. The town's lodging tax shows when guests come: in 2024, almost 6 in 10 of its dollars came in from July to September, and about 2 in 100 from January to March.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Winter days are mild.</p><ul class="c3-pi-stats" aria-label="A January day"><li><b>About 57°</b><span>January's normal high</span></li><li><b>About 37°</b><span>January's normal low</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those are NOAA's normals at its weather station at Brookgreen Gardens, about 6 miles north. From October through April, dogs may run on the beach off the leash, if the owner carries one and the dog comes when called. Winter is also outside hurricane season, which runs from June 1 to November 30.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That makes winter the easiest time for work on a house: rentals are fewest and the storm season is over.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Behind the island and west of the highway, about 3 in 4 houses or more are their owner's main home. On the island about 1 in 5 is.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses that are their owner's main home, by part"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses that are their owner's main home, by part</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.206" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.414" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mainland behind the island</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.733" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 3 in 4</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.857" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 6 in 7</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses taxed at the main-home rate in Georgetown County's 2026 tax records. The rest are second homes and rentals.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A South Carolina beach</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tax bills for most island houses go to South Carolina addresses: about a quarter to Pawleys Island itself, and many to Columbia, Greenville and Charleston. About 3 in 10 go out of state.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Where the tax bills for island houses go"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Where the tax bills for island houses go</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">City</span><span role="columnheader">Houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.888" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">127 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Columbia</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.231" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">33 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Greenville</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.189" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">27 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Charleston</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.14" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">20 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Georgetown</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.091" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mount Pleasant</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.084" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">12 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Florence</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.07" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">10 houses</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Out of state</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">143 houses</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The mailing city on each island house's tax bill, Georgetown County records. A mailing city is where the bill goes, not always where the owner lives. Out of state, North Carolina, Georgia, Tennessee and Virginia lead.</figcaption></figure><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/pawleys-island-beach-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden walkway over green dunes leading to the ocean on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A wooden walkway over the dunes to the beach on Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from Town Hall on the island, without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 adds time.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From Town Hall to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The nearest grocery store, on US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Under 5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Hammock Shops, on US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Huntington Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Brookgreen Gardens</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Downtown Georgetown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">40 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach, Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">40 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Downtown Charleston</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1 hr 45 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Schools are assigned by address in the Georgetown County School District, and we look up the assigned schools for any house you like. The town has its own police department.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where to eat</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town says island night life is dining out, long talks on screened porches, a mainland shop and a walk on the beach. On the map we count 20 restaurants from Litchfield south past the causeways, and 19 of them are within about 650 feet of US 17. Among them are the Pawleys Island Tavern, Frank's and Frank's Outback, and Local at the Hammock Shops.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-often"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How often one sells">How often does a house on Pawleys Island come up for sale?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rarely. In the past five years at least 44 of the island's 480 houses were bought at a market price, about 1 in 11. In Litchfield and west of the highway, houses were bought about twice as often.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses bought at a market price in the past five years"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses bought at a market price in the past five years</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.368" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 11</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.74" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.784" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 5</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>At least: the county keeps only the last deed on each house, so a house sold and later deeded to a trust counts as not sold. That is true in every part. Georgetown County records; a market sale is a deed of $10,000 or more.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Island houses tend to stay in families. On most of them, the last recorded transfer was not a sale. The deed shows under $1,000: the kind of deed used to pass a house to heirs or a trust, or to move it into a company.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses whose last recorded transfer was not a sale"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses whose last recorded transfer was not a sale</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part</span><span role="columnheader">Share of houses</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island, the town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.615" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 6 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Litchfield, ocean side of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.405" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West of US 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.329" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 3</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The last deed on the house shows under $1,000. Georgetown County records.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town says many houses in its historic district belong to the third, fourth or fifth generation of one family. About 1 in 10 island houses has not changed hands at all since before 2000. The island is also built out: in seven years, only about a dozen new buildings went up.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What it means for you: the house you want can come up once in years.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want a house on the island?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the part of the island, the size and your budget. We watch the island and call you when a house like it comes up.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us to watch for a house on Pawleys Island</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="history"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The old houses">Why do the old Pawleys Island houses look the way they do?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The old Pawleys Island houses were built as summer houses for rice planters' families, who came from May to November to escape the malaria of the rice fields. Enslaved people carried the households to the island each May, and enslaved workers built the older of the two causeways under a rice planter who became governor.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cypress was the building material used most often. It was hewn on the mainland, and each timber was cut with Roman numerals so the house could be put together on the island. Most of the old houses stand on high brick foundations, which keep them above ordinary storm tides and let air move under the floor.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle of the island is on the National Register of Historic Places as the Pawleys Island Historic District.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The town's historic rules</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 2026 the whole island became a local historic district. A house built in 1954 or earlier can be put on the town's list of historic houses. The owner can nominate it, and so can a member of the town council or of the town's board, so a house can be nominated without its owner asking. The council decides.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A listed house needs the board's approval for changes to its outside and to be torn down, and the board can delay a demolition for up to 180 days. The listing stays with the house when it sells. No building permit is issued while a nomination is pending. A house not on the list has none of these rules. We check whether a house you like is listed or nominated.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="taxes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly costs">What does a Pawleys Island house cost to own each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The biggest yearly costs are property tax and insurance. Both depend most on whether the house is your main home.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Property tax</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">As a second home or rental, a house pays about 3 times the property tax it pays as the home you live in. South Carolina taxes the home you live in on 4 percent of its value and any other house on 6 percent, and the tax rate on a second home is also about twice as high.</p><div class="c3-pi-tax"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Price</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Main home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Second home</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$580,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,740</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$8,350</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$900,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,150</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$12,850</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,450,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$11,220</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$34,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tax a year, from Georgetown County's own estimate. $580,000 is the middle sale west of US 17, and $2,450,000 the island's. A second home here includes a rental.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The estimate includes the fees on the bill. The fees are $44 a year on the island. West of the highway they are $96, for storm water and household fees together. The county taxes its own appraised value, which can differ from the price. The Town of Pawleys Island levies no property tax of its own, so an island house pays the same rates as the mainland around it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood insurance</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A federal flood policy on an island house that is not its owner's main home cost more than 4 times what one on a mainland house in the same ZIP code cost. As a main home, the gap is much smaller. The town's flood work earns island owners a 25 percent discount on these policies, and the prices below already include it.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a federal flood policy on a house cost a year, at the middle</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">House</span><span role="columnheader">A year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, not the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,770</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Island house, the owner's main home</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.353" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,680</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mainland house, same ZIP code</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.22" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,050</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>FEMA's flood insurance policies on single-family houses that began in the 12 months to May 2026, ZIP 29585. Island: the Town of Pawleys Island's policies. Mainland: the Georgetown County policies in the same ZIP code. The cost includes FEMA's fees.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most island policies cover the building for $250,000, the most the federal program pays on a home. A house worth more needs private flood coverage on top. Wind and homeowners insurance come on top of that. Their prices depend on the house's height, age and roof, so we get quotes on the house before you offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: the island's middle house as a second home</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take an island house at the middle price that you keep as a second home or rent out. Before the mortgage, and before wind and homeowners insurance, it costs about $39,700 a year.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax as a second home, with the $44 in fees</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$34,900</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A federal flood policy, the middle for an island house that is not a main home</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,770</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Together</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$39,700</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the yearly cost of the Pawleys house you like</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its tax as a main home and a second home, and get its insurance quotes before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out a house's yearly cost</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you rent out a house on Pawleys Island, and what do rentals take in?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Short-term rentals are allowed on Pawleys Island. Guests pay about 11 percent in lodging taxes on stays under 90 days. The town's share is filed with the town each month.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's lodging tax receipts show what island rentals take in. In 2024, guests paid about $27 million to stay on the island. Spread across the roughly 380 island houses that are not an owner's main home, that is about $70,000 a house for the year, before the rental company's fee and other costs.</p><ul class="c3-pi-stats" aria-label="Island rentals in a year"><li><b>About $27 million</b><span>Rent guests paid on the island in a year</span></li><li><b>About $70,000</b><span>A year, on average, per house that is not a main home</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That is an average. Some houses are never rented, and some of the rent is paid on the island's condos and other rooms.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the mainland, a homeowners association can limit rentals in its own papers, and we read them for you. The rules town by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>. For a yearly tenant instead, see our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">long-term rental guide</a>. If you are selling a rental elsewhere to buy here, a <a href="/invest/strategies/1031-exchange/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">1031 exchange</a> can put off the tax on the sale.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding and storms">Does Pawleys Island flood, and how often do hurricanes come?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every island house but one is in one of FEMA's high-risk flood zones. A lender making a mortgage on any of them will require flood insurance. The island's houses are split about evenly between two zones:</p><ul class="c3-pi-rules"><li><strong>About half: water and waves</strong>Rising water and storm waves are both expected here. FEMA calls it the VE zone.</li><li><strong>The other half: water</strong>Water rises in a big flood, but big waves are not expected. FEMA calls it the AE zone.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The south end is the most exposed. South of the South Causeway, more than 9 in 10 houses are in the VE zone. North of the North Causeway, fewer than 1 in 10 are.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA's flood height for island houses is 12 to 16 feet. It is measured from a fixed survey level, not from the ground, so it is not the depth of water at a house. The town requires the floor of a new house to sit 3 feet above that.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On ordinary days, the town's flood problem is water on the roads at the highest tides of the year, the king tides. The town has adopted a drainage plan for the whole island to deal with it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Hurricanes</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past 75 years, 44 storms have passed within 50 miles of the middle of the island, and 7 of them were hurricanes at their closest point. Ian passed about 5 miles away, and Matthew and Charley came closer still.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-pi-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Storms that passed within 50 miles of the island, by decade</span><svg class="c3-pi-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 240" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of storms whose center passed within 50 miles of Pawleys Island, by decade: 1950s 5 storms, 2 hurricanes; 1960s 5 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1970s 2 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1980s 4 storms, 0 hurricanes; 1990s 4 storms, 0 hurricanes; 2000s 8 storms, 1 hurricanes; 2010s 8 storms, 2 hurricanes; 2020s 8 storms, 2 hurricanes."><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="196" y2="196" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="28" y="202" text-anchor="end">0</text><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="111" y2="111" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="28" y="117" text-anchor="end">5</text><line x1="34" x2="352" y1="26" y2="26" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="28" y="32" text-anchor="end">10</text><rect x="39.6" y="111" width="28.6" height="85" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="39.6" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="53.9" y="105" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text x="53.9" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’50</text><rect x="79.3" y="111" width="28.6" height="85" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="93.6" y="105" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text x="93.6" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’60</text><rect x="119.1" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="133.4" y="156" text-anchor="middle">2</text><text x="133.4" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’70</text><rect x="158.8" y="128" width="28.6" height="68" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="173.1" y="122" text-anchor="middle">4</text><text x="173.1" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’80</text><rect x="198.6" y="128" width="28.6" height="68" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text class="v" x="212.9" y="122" text-anchor="middle">4</text><text x="212.9" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’90</text><rect x="238.3" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="238.3" y="179" width="28.6" height="17" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="252.6" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="252.6" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’00</text><rect x="278.1" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="278.1" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="292.4" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="292.4" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’10</text><rect x="317.8" y="60" width="28.6" height="136" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="317.8" y="162" width="28.6" height="34" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text class="v" x="332.1" y="54" text-anchor="middle">8</text><text x="332.1" y="222" text-anchor="middle">’20</text></svg><ul class="c3-pi-names" aria-label="The seven hurricanes"><li>Hazel, 1954</li><li>Helene, 1958</li><li>Charley, 2004</li><li>Matthew, 2016</li><li>Dorian, 2019</li><li>Isaias, 2020</li><li>Ian, 2022</li></ul><figcaption>Each column is a decade, from the 1950s (’50) to the 2020s (’20). Darker: storms that were hurricanes at their closest point. NOAA National Hurricane Center storm tracks (HURDAT2), 1950 to 2025, measured from the middle of the island.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hurricane Hazel, in 1954, washed away most of the houses built on the south end after World War II. The older houses came through it, as they had come through many storms before.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the flood zone and floor height of one Pawleys house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We look up its flood zone, VE or AE, and how high its floor is above the flood height on FEMA's map.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a house's flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="rebuild"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Building on the ocean">Can you rebuild an oceanfront house on Pawleys Island?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, within limits that matter most at the south end. The state draws two lines along the beach. The baseline follows the top of the front dune. The setback line runs 20 feet behind it, on the land side.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On about 100 of the island's roughly 220 oceanfront houses, part of the house stands on the ocean side of the setback line. Most of them are at the south end. On Litchfield's oceanfront it is more than half of the houses.</p><figure class="c3-pi-fig narrow"><div class="c3-pi-frame"><svg class="c3-pi-inset" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="650 250 850 900" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-pi-inset-t"><title id="c3-pi-inset-t">Aerial map of the south end of Pawleys Island: one row of oceanfront houses between the creek and the beach. The state's baseline along the top of the front dune and its setback line 20 feet behind it run through the row of houses. A shaded house has part of it on the ocean side of the setback line.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-south-end-aerial-1000.webp" x="650" y="250" width="850" height="900" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1383.2 -50.9L1376.4 -38.1L1377 -37.7L1368.8 -22.6L1370 -22.2L1366.9 -16.5L1379 -9.8L1381.5 -15.2L1406.5 -1.7L1412.4 -13.1L1416.9 -10.8L1414.1 -5.4L1416.9 -4L1418.3 -6.4L1430.2 0L1433 -5.1L1413.8 -15.2L1415.3 -17.9L1409.3 -20.9L1409.9 -21.9L1408.5 -22.6L1414.7 -34.4L1383.2 -50.9Z" fill="rgba(196,120,58,.5)" stroke="#ffb35c" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M1402 13.1L1368.6 -6.1L1368.3 -5.7L1362.1 -9.1L1360.1 -5.1L1354.8 -8.1L1348.6 3.7L1353.9 6.4L1344.9 23.6L1385.2 44.8L1389.4 36.7L1395.8 40.1L1400.1 32.3L1404 35L1402 38.7L1405.1 40.4L1407.4 37.4L1424 47.5L1425.9 44.1L1401.7 29L1405.7 21.9L1400.9 19.5L1399.5 22.2L1397.5 21.2L1402 13.1Z" fill="rgba(196,120,58,.5)" stroke="#ffb35c" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M1342.4 42.4L1324.1 76.1L1356.7 93.6L1364.6 78.8L1369.7 81.5L1366.3 87.9L1379 94.3L1381.2 89.6L1384.6 91.3L1386.3 88.3L1395.8 93L1397.5 89.9L1385.2 82.5L1390.5 71.7L1380.4 66.4L1382.1 63.3L1342.4 42.4Z" fill="rgba(196,120,58,.5)" stroke="#ffb35c" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M1318.5 92L1299.1 129.7L1330.6 14